+## A beforeSession that throws
+
+- A `beforeSession` that throws still reaches the caller as the same rejection, and `onError` fires for that throw with the session and the very error thrown — the same argument shape any other orchestrator failure delivers ([validated by: rejects with the thrown error and hands it to onError like any other failure](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L43)).
+- `afterSession` fires for that throw too, after `onError`, so a hook releasing what `beforeSession` allocated runs on exactly the path where the allocation failed; it can assume only that the turn began and ended — no provider call, no other hook, and no entry committed — and reads anything finer from the session it is handed ([validated by: still runs afterSession, after onError, though no part of the turn happened](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L66)).
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
